(a) The city manager or his/her designee shall have the discretion to grant or refuse to grant any application for a license hereunder; however, the city manager or his/her designee shall consider the following matters in connection with each application for a license hereunder, which considerations are deemed to be in the public interest and welfare, as follows:
(1) Whether the applicant, or any person having a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the issuance of the license, has had any license issued by the city or by any other city in the state, or by any other licensing authority in the state relating to the manufacture, distribution or sale of alcoholic beverages suspended within the past five (5) years or revoked within the past ten (10) years;
(2) Whether any applicant for a license to manufacture and/or sell distilled spirits or package beer and wine, or any person having a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the issuance of the license, has had any license issued by the city or by any other city in the state, or by any other licensing authority in the state relating to the manufacture, distribution or sale of alcoholic beverages suspended within the past five (5) years or revoked within the past ten (10) years;
(3) Whether the applicant or any person owning a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the license for which application is made has sufficient mental capacity to conduct the business for which the application is made;
(4) Whether the applicant or any person owning a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the license for which application is made fails to demonstrate financial stability;
(5) Whether the applicant is twenty-one (21) years of age or older;
(6) Whether the applicant is a citizen of the United States or a resident alien lawfully permitted for permanent residence;
(7) Whether the location of the premises from which the proposed sale of alcoholic beverages shall be conducted meets the distance restrictions set forth by state law and local ordinance;
(8) The applicant's reputation, character, criminal history, and mental and physical capacity to conduct the business proposed to be conducted;
(9) Whether the applicant has been convicted of, pled guilty to, or entered a plea of nolo contendre to, or is presently charged with any felony, any misdemeanor involving moral turpitude, any criminal offense relating to lottery rules or regulations, any offense related to illegal gambling, soliciting for prostitution, pandering, letting of premises for prostitution, keeping a disorderly place, any offense related to the illegal possession or sale of illegal drugs or alcoholic beverages, any sex offense found in O.C.G.A. Title 16, Chapter 6 or any similar violation found in any other state or federal statute, any charges related to the manufacture or sale of alcoholic beverages, or a second offense of driving under the influence of alcohol within the last ten (10) years;
(10) Whether the applicant, or any person who shall have a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the license, as a previous holder of a license to manufacture and/or sell any type of alcoholic beverages has been found to have violated any law, regulation or ordinance relating to such business within a ten-year period, immediately preceding the date of the application for license hereunder;
(11) If applicant is a previous holder of a license to manufacture and/or sell any type of alcoholic beverages, the manner in which he or she conducted the business under such license and the necessity for any unusual police observation and inspection of such prior business in order to prevent the violation of any law, regulation or ordinance relating to such business;
(12) If applicant has had a prior license, whether any such prior license for the manufacture and/or sale of any type of alcoholic beverages has been suspended or revoked or whether or not hearings have been held for the revocation or suspension of any such license regardless of whether or not any such license was revoked or suspended as a result of such hearing;
(13) The location of the premises from which the proposed manufacture and/or sale of alcoholic beverages shall be conducted;
(14) Whether the applicant, or any person who shall have a direct or indirect beneficial interest in the license, has had any city license revoked within two (2) years prior to the filing of the application;
(15) Whether the facility where the applicant proposes to manufacture and/or sell alcoholic beverages meets city zoning requirements;
(16) Whether it appears that the applicant would have adequate financial participation in the proposed business to direct and manage its affairs, or whether it appears that the applicant is intended to be a mere surrogate for a person or persons who would not otherwise qualify for a license for any reason whatsoever; and
(17) Whether the applicant has failed to meet any other criteria specified by this chapter or state law.
(b) The city manager or his/her designee has discretionary authority to consider any other objective criteria that is rationally related to the application including any extenuating circumstances which may reflect favorably or unfavorably on the applicant, application, or the proposed location of the business when making a decision to approve or deny a license requested hereunder. If, in the judgment of the city manager or his/her designee, circumstances are such that granting the license would not be in the best interest of the general health, safety, and public welfare, such circumstances shall be grounds for denying the application.
(Ord. No. 2026-14, § 3(Exh. A), 7-7-26)

